Define __builtin_offsetof, GCC's name for offsetof.

C written for GCC and TinyCC both, as the Rach2 kernel is, spells
offsetof as GCC's stddef.h does, __builtin_offsetof(type, member), and
TinyCC 0.9.27 knew no such name, so `offsetof(struct x, m)` there was a
call of an undeclared function and a syntax error after it. The name is
now defined as the expression TinyCC's own stddef.h gives offsetof.

--- a/libtcc.c
+++ b/libtcc.c
@@ -779,6 +779,10 @@ LIBTCCAPI TCCState *tcc_new(void)
     tcc_define_symbol(s, "__STDC__", NULL);
     tcc_define_symbol(s, "__STDC_VERSION__", "199901L");
     tcc_define_symbol(s, "__STDC_HOSTED__", NULL);
+    /* GCC's name for the offsetof of stddef.h, which C code that targets
+       both compilers spells */
+    tcc_define_symbol(s, "__builtin_offsetof(type, field)",
+                      "((__SIZE_TYPE__)&((type *)0)->field)");
 
     /* target defines */
 #if defined(TCC_TARGET_I386)
